  "id": "Compound::DB00526 - Gene::9429",
  "verbalization": "Oxaliplatin and Abcg2 are linked through a shared pathway involving platinum-containing compounds, which are bound to Abcg2. The evidence suggests that Oxaliplatin, whether as part of Carboplatin or Cisplatin, binds to Gstt1, which in turn interacts with Carboplatin or Cisplatin to ultimately reach Abcg2. This creates a network of interactions where Oxaliplatin indirectly influences Abcg2 through its inclusion in platinum-based compounds. The lowest common ancestors of Oxaliplatin and Carboplatin, as well as Oxaliplatin and Cisplatin, both point to Platinum Compound or Platinum Coordination Entity, reinforcing the role of platinum-based drugs in mediating the interaction with Abcg2. The mechanism appears to involve a coordinated pathway where Oxaliplatin's presence in platinum compounds triggers a series of binding events that culminate in the interaction with Abcg2.",
